    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "28 and 16.",
      "worked": "Let the larger number be $x$. The smaller number is $x-12$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+(x-12)&=44\\\\2x-12&=44\\\\2x&=56\\\\x&=28\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe smaller number is $28-12=16$.\n\nThe numbers are 28 and 16.\n\nCheck: $28-16=12$ and $28+16=44$.",
